Rebuilding a process's PMP image counts one entry more than its filled region slots,
which loads an entry past the image and, with every slot filled, more entries than the process has room for.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: PMP image grants rights the slots do not
Report: PMP image has more entries than the process has region slots

diff --git a/kernel/process.c b/kernel/process.c
--- a/kernel/process.c
+++ b/kernel/process.c
@@ -61,7 +61,7 @@ static void rebuild_pmp(struct process *proc)
             count++;
         }
     }
-    proc->pmp_count = (uint8_t)count;
+    proc->pmp_count = (uint8_t)(count + 1);
     const struct thread *current = core_self()->current;
     if (current != NULL && thread_process(current) == proc) {
         process_activate(proc);
